<h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
<p class="muted">What you get when you buy a design, how the license works, how custom orders run, and how to heal the tattoo afterwards — answered plainly.</p>

<p>Most questions about Tattoo Art Customs come down to one thing: this is a marketplace for tattoo <em>artwork</em>, not a tattoo parlor, and that confuses people until somebody explains it once. You buy finished, tattoo-ready files — the full-color artwork and the clean linework your artist stencils from — together with a license to have that design tattooed on you once. Everything below expands on that: the license in plain language, the custom-order process step by step, sizing and aging honesty, aftercare essentials, and how artists and shops fit in. If your question is not answered here, <a href="/contact">contact us</a> and a human will answer it.</p>

<% faqs.forEach(function(f) { %>
<section class="card">
  <h2><%= f.q %></h2>
  <% f.a.forEach(function(p) { %><p><%- p %></p><% }); %>
</section>
<% }); %>

<section class="card">
  <h2>Still deciding?</h2>
  <p>Browse the <a href="/gallery">design gallery</a> when you know the subject but not the style, read the <a href="/styles">style guides</a> when you know the style but not the subject, or go straight to a <a href="/orders/custom">custom order</a> when the piece only exists in your head. After the appointment, the <a href="/guides/aftercare">aftercare guide</a> takes it from there.</p>
</section>
